<http://data.silknow.org/object/65ddabe3-c649-3265-bcbc-bb6d37e21091>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Embroidered panel showing two lilies worked in gold, beige, cream and ivory-coloured silks mostly in stem stitch on a pale gold coloured satin ground. Lined with a yellow silk damask showing a repeating design of bats with outstretched wings against a cloudy sky with stars and moon."@en , "Embroidered panel of satin, England, ca. 1890"@en ;
